pkghaus-archive-keyring (2026.09.11) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Ship the source-signing key B04D491E3C0209F8C2F7B1F05B88ED4C9FF690E5 in a
    second keyring at /usr/share/keyrings/pkghaus-source-keyring.gpg. It signs
    .dsc files, and its public half has to reach users before the first signed
    source package exists.
  * Keep it out of pkghaus-archive-keyring.gpg. apt accepts any signing key in
    the keyring a Signed-By line names, so a source-signing key in the trust
    anchor could sign a Release that every client accepts, and that key sits on
    every build leg of every package. The archive keyring is unchanged.
  * The build and the DEP-8 test each assert that a keyring carries its own
    signing subkey and not the other one. verify-key now walks every subkey
    instead of the first, which would have stopped checking as soon as a
    rotation put two of them in one keyring.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 17:45:01 +0200
pkghaus-archive-keyring (2026.09.02.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Build from the key in this directory instead of cloning an archived
    repository. keys/pkg.haus-archive.asc stayed behind in
    pkghaus/archive-keyring when the packaging moved here, and that repository
    was archived: read-only clones kept working so builds never failed, but the
    key could no longer be changed and the documented rotation procedure could
    not be carried out at all. The keyring itself is unchanged and the binary is
    byte-identical to 2026.09.02; only where the key is kept has moved.
  * Declare no upstream. A native package's source is its own directory, and
    action-debian-build v1.5.0 refuses UPSTREAM and VERSION on one.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 15:19:57 +0200

pkghaus-archive-keyring (2026.09.02) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Give gpg a home inside the build tree. It writes a keybox into GNUPGHOME,
    which pointed at a $HOME the build had no claim on.
  * Build reproducibly: identical bytes across build path, hostname, locale,
    timezone, umask, CPU count and file ordering.
  * Publish this version's source package and build record at
    buildinfos.pkg.haus, so anyone can reproduce the build and check it.

 -- pkg.haus archive <archive@pkg.haus>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 11:38:12 +0200

